ber/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:23:35-07:00","id":594913,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/The-Fall-act-zero-page-4-547258798\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Th...ge-4-547258798</a> page four of &quot;The Fall, act zero&quot;. A different face is shown!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:44:39-07:00","id":595380,"title":"","content":"Hm...black silhouettes for crowd scenes. Bit more menacing than I'm usually going for with Boot, but I may toy with the crowd-as-silhouette method. I keep having scenes full of people (the Rain Festival, this martial arts tournament) but not having the time or enthusiasm to draw dozens and dozens of extras. A little bit of copy-paste goes a long way, but I don't wanna overuse it. This is an elegant solution.<br /> <br /> I compliment you again on your ridiculous output (seriously, you draw so much in so little time!) and on the continuing improvement that's showing in your work. I'm loving the lightsaber claws in this one, and your writing is getting better too. I keep trying to cramp too much text into a single page. Reading your stuff is a good reminder that I can relax and slow down a bit, it'll flow better in the archive that way.<br /> <br /> So thank you for your continual updates without much in the way of feedback! Consider this your quarterly reminder that at least one of us is reading and enjoying your comic! Keep it up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T03:41:56-07:00","id":595531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/334307-webcomic-tales-of-exalts?p=595380#post595380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...black silhouettes for crowd scenes. Bit more menacing than I'm usually going for with Boot, but I may toy with the crowd-as-silhouette method. I keep having scenes full of people (the Rain Festival, this martial arts tournament) but not having the time or enthusiasm to draw dozens and dozens of extras. A little bit of copy-paste goes a long way, but I don't wanna overuse it. This is an elegant solution.<br /> <br /> I compliment you again on your ridiculous output (seriously, you draw so much in so little time!) and on the continuing improvement that's showing in your work. I'm loving the lightsaber claws in this one, and your writing is getting better too. I keep trying to cramp too much text into a single page. Reading your stuff is a good reminder that I can relax and slow down a bit, it'll flow better in the archive that way.<br /> <br /> So thank you for your continual updates without much in the way of feedback! Consider this your quarterly reminder that at least one of us is reading and enjoying your comic! Keep it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you for the comment Guru, it means a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> hmmm lets see here, well i think that the silhouette technique might work for you depending on how dark you make them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise one trick that the comic artist that inspired me to start making my webcomic, Fred Perry, often use for background characters is to pretty much only draw their rough shapes (a couple of &quot;internal lines&quot; for things like clothes and armor but no real detail lines), and then fill it with a desaturated dark color (not super dark like black but just a bit darker than usual, blue and purple works well for this, however depending on the background sometimes you can use a slight variation on the background color instead).<br /> <br /> Another trick that might work for you is to do similar to the previous trick and draw the rough shapes, but with a bit more detail and instead of using a desaturated color, you use your &quot;flats&quot; colors without actually rendering them, making them look almost a bit faceless (this might turn out a bit strange though if the background character is to close but it works if they are a bit further away).<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to try with the silhouettes technique at first, just to get a feel on how they work, if they feel ok to you then i suggest that you use them for background characters that are placed &quot;in front&quot; of the characters you want to have in focus since unless they are 100% black opacity they should be a lot less &quot;eye catching&quot; than the &quot;focus&quot; characters.<br /> They can also be used for background characters that are farther away.<br /> <br /> the same trick can be used for the second technique i mentioned, you can also try to draw a &quot;blob&quot; when it's a tightly packed crowd and then add a few heads to the &quot;blob&quot; trimming it a bit to make it feel a bit more &quot;natural&quot;.<br /> <br /> the final technique I suggest using for when characters stand a bit closer, though not for characters that are standing in front of your &quot;focus&quot; characters since that might draw attention away from what you want people to focus on, this technique can also be used on more important characters that are standing farther away though you may want to give those character a bit of rendering.<br /> Also if it is a character that is very bright like lets say that you at some point draw a scene where someone's being chased by a fire aspect in full anima and you want the fire aspect to be visible but the focus to be on the one that he/she is chasing, i suggest that you use desaturate the bright colors so it become's a bit less eye catching.<br /> <br /> I hope that these tricks will be of some use to you since i know how annoying and tiresome background crowds are to draw and i hope i made sense, if I didn't let me know and I will try to make better sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> oh and one more hint is to actually copy paste a few slightly more detailed background characters characters, (maybe mirror them so they are looking in another direction or something similar) and then &quot;merge&quot; them with the silhouette crowd.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the compliment, it is really encouraging and motivating to hear that, yup i like his claws too, i took the opportunity to add a tiny Easter egg in it's sound effects.<br /> Aaaaah the curse of &quot;I have so much i need to say in too few panels&quot; I did that a lot in chapter 5 of tales of exalts. Poor Ekorren had to go through those walls of texts (he helps me with the grammar/spelling when he has the time so huge thanks to Ekorren). It makes me happy that you feel that way, it is good that i can help in my own way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> YAY, (over the internet friendship hug) it means A LOT to me to know that I have at least a couple of readers and that at least one of them is enjoying it, and I will make sure to keep on working especially after getting grand motivators like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I hope I make sense and haven't misspelled or butchered the grammar to much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T05:35:39-07:00","id":596782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/The-Fall-act-zero-page-5-547643620\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Th...ge-5-547643620</a> page five of &quot;The Fall, act zero&quot;. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">as one fall, more arrive</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5